  "prefLabel": "Ahp 210.03 Roles of Complainants and Board Staff",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ahp 210.03 Roles of Complainants and Board Staff.\n\n(a) Complainants alleging misconduct by a licensed or certified individual shall have no role in any hearing other than that of witness unless they petition for, and are granted, the right to intervene.\n\n(b) Unless called as witnesses, board staff shall have no role in any hearing.\n\nSource. #7232, eff 4-15-00; ss by #8078, eff 5-1-04; ss by #9833, eff 12-15-10",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ahp100-600.html"
}
